 "summary": "The Lean theorem proves an algebraic vector identity over any field R. If n, a ∈ R³ with n·n ≠ 0 and n·a = 0, then (−1/(n·n))·(n×(n×a)) = a. This is the triple-product (BAC−CAB) identity specialised to a ⊥ n. The paper text labelled Lemma 8.8 is a quite different result: it computes the radial remainder R_g and the updated defects (P, J_θ, J_z) after a mean correction, and gives their M/S-class membership. The pairing is therefore a mismatch caused by the candidate-manuscript numbering. The Lean statement is correct for what it says, but it does not formalize the shown Lemma 8.8.",
